-- WITHAL after the name of a type that is not a record: only a term can be
-- built, so this is the ordinary "could not find a definition" error and
-- nothing about WITHAL (TYPICALLY-ONE-BEHAVIOUR-SPEC.md T1, ruled by Meng
-- 2026-10-09). The message carries the checker's inference counter, so the
-- test looks for its words and not its digits.
DECLARE Colour IS ONE OF Red, Green

#EVAL Colour WITHAL
